{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "task_family": "incremental_english_modern_japanese_overlay",
  "book_id": "no-longer-human",
  "chunk_id": "no-longer-human-chunk-0205",
  "units": [
    {
      "paragraph_id": "no-longer-human-zh-p00205",
      "unit_index": 1,
      "source_text": "當時我還發明瞭另一種類似的遊戲，那就是反義詞的猜字遊戲。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "At the time, I had also invented another similar game: a guessing game of antonyms.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "no-longer-human-zh-p00205",
      "unit_index": 2,
      "source_text": "比如黑的反詞（反義詞的略稱）是白，白的反義詞卻是紅，紅的反義詞是黑。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "For example, the opposite of black, or anto for short, is white; but the opposite of white is red, and the opposite of red is black.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "no-longer-human-zh-p00205",
      "unit_index": 3,
      "source_text": "「花的反詞是？」我這麼一問，堀木噘著嘴想了一下。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "When I asked, \"What is the opposite of flower?\" Horiki pursed his lips and thought for a moment.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "no-longer-human-zh-p00205",
      "unit_index": 4,
      "source_text": "「嗯，有一家叫花月的餐館，那就是月。」",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "\"Hmm, there is a restaurant called Kagetsu, Flower Moon, so it must be moon.\"",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "no-longer-human-zh-p00205",
      "unit_index": 5,
      "source_text": "「不對，它不能稱為反詞。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "\"No, that cannot be called an opposite.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "no-longer-human-zh-p00205",
      "unit_index": 6,
      "source_text": "不如說是同義詞。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "If anything, it is a synonym.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "no-longer-human-zh-p00205",
      "unit_index": 7,
      "source_text": "星星和紫羅蘭不就是同義詞嗎？",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "Aren't stars and violets synonyms too?",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "no-longer-human-zh-p00205",
      "unit_index": 8,
      "source_text": "它不是反詞。」",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "It is not an opposite.\"",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "no-longer-human-zh-p00205",
      "unit_index": 9,
      "source_text": "「我明白了，那就是蜜蜂。」",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "\"I understand now; it is a bee.\"",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "no-longer-human-zh-p00205",
      "unit_index": 10,
      "source_text": "「蜜蜂？」「牡丹上……螞蟻？」",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "\"A bee?\" \"On a peony... an ant?\"",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "no-longer-human-zh-p00205",
      "unit_index": 11,
      "source_text": "「什麼呀，那是繪畫的主題。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "\"What are you talking about? That is a subject for a painting.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "no-longer-human-zh-p00205",
      "unit_index": 12,
      "source_text": "你別想打馬虎眼。」",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "Do not try to dodge the question.\"",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
